WEBVTT

00:16.510 --> 00:19.410
Taiyou ni me ga kurameba

00:19.410 --> 00:24.090
hikari no hate o shiru darou

00:24.090 --> 00:25.990
Hoshikuzu no nou

00:25.990 --> 00:31.830
Nante semai uchuu de boku wa ikiteru

00:31.830 --> 00:39.370
Dare ka zero kara hajimeru
koodo o sazukete kurenai ka

00:39.370 --> 00:41.940
Zoushoku sare sakuran

00:41.940 --> 00:45.970
Hako no naka shiseru koronii

00:45.970 --> 00:50.450
Kakan naki yume o ute

00:50.450 --> 00:53.620
Kodoku yo jibaku seyo

00:53.620 --> 00:58.020
Yubisaki no mirai ni

00:58.020 --> 01:01.860
donna sakurifaisu ga arou to

01:01.860 --> 01:05.530
Mune no oku de

01:05.530 --> 01:08.830
Kokoro koushin seyo

01:08.830 --> 01:12.970
Ippo kako no hibi ga

01:12.970 --> 01:15.970
toozakatte yukedomo

01:15.970 --> 01:23.040
Koishikarubeki kimi

01:40.900 --> 01:43.430
There are two kinds of worlds.

01:43.430 --> 01:44.900
Worlds that die out on their own...

01:44.900 --> 01:48.370
and worlds that are purposely destroyed.

01:48.370 --> 01:50.840
Hey, why are you standing all the
way up there trying to act cool?

01:50.840 --> 01:52.900
You know you're a bear, right?

01:53.410 --> 01:56.510
I am a hero... and I won't
dignify that with an answer.

01:56.510 --> 01:59.280
More to the point, what's our plan?

01:59.280 --> 02:02.620
It's been a while since the fuel ran out.

02:02.620 --> 02:04.390
And besides, I'm hungry.

02:04.390 --> 02:05.920
Nothing to worry about.

02:05.920 --> 02:09.860
This is supposed to show us
the path to world destruction.

02:09.860 --> 02:13.060
Oh yeah? That thing acts as a compass too?

02:13.060 --> 02:15.600
Of course, we're all probably
gonna die of starvation right here

02:15.600 --> 02:18.770
before we even get to world destruction...

02:18.770 --> 02:22.140
But wait! Maybe that thing has
some kind of a can opener on it?

02:22.140 --> 02:23.710
Yeah right... as if!

02:23.710 --> 02:28.080
Destroying the world is
the only thing it can do.

02:28.080 --> 02:29.940
But people always say more is better!

02:29.940 --> 02:32.750
What do you think you're doing?! Give it back!

02:32.750 --> 02:36.420
How the heck did I get myself into this?

02:36.420 --> 02:38.290
I never would've thought a hero like me

02:38.290 --> 02:42.120
could fall into the hands of these
World Destruction Committee goofballs.

02:42.120 --> 02:46.630
Here's where I do something
about that Destruct Code.

02:46.630 --> 02:50.660
Hey guys, canned food is all well and
good, but can we open this bottle first?

02:54.070 --> 02:57.840
Another sand octopus?!
Or maybe a sand whale this time?!

03:00.080 --> 03:02.810
No, that's a World
Salvation Committee subarenine!

03:02.810 --> 03:04.680
"Subarenine"?

03:06.110 --> 03:08.420
We finally found 'em by sheer luck!

03:08.420 --> 03:09.780
Fire!

03:09.780 --> 03:11.320
But what about the Destruct Code?

03:11.320 --> 03:13.860
Our little torpedoes ain't
gonna do nothin' to that thing!

03:13.860 --> 03:16.990
We'll just go get it from
their dead bodies afterwards.

03:16.990 --> 03:18.860
Now shut up and let 'er rip!

03:23.970 --> 03:25.500
They're shooting already?!

03:25.500 --> 03:27.000
Abandon ship, bear-o!

03:27.000 --> 03:28.330
Bear-o!

03:38.050 --> 03:43.010
"There are Two Kinds of Worlds"

03:48.720 --> 03:52.190
I don't see any dead bodies.
No Destruct Code, either.

03:52.190 --> 03:53.960
They must've escaped.

03:53.960 --> 03:55.830
But they couldn't have gone far!

03:55.830 --> 03:59.800
Call up more World Salvation
Committee forces and search the whole area!

03:59.800 --> 04:00.790
Yessir!

04:13.410 --> 04:15.680
And now we bid our final farewell.

04:34.540 --> 04:36.370
Morte...

04:54.020 --> 04:55.850
Are you awake?

04:58.960 --> 04:59.890
Where am I?

04:59.890 --> 05:01.630
You're on my sand ship.

05:01.630 --> 05:03.600
This man helped us.

05:03.600 --> 05:08.700
You were clinging to a board and
floating helplessly on this vast Sand Sea.

05:08.700 --> 05:12.310
If I hadn't found you, all three
of you'd probably be in the belly

05:12.310 --> 05:14.940
of some sand snake at the
bottom of the sea by now.

05:16.980 --> 05:19.310
Thank you.

05:19.310 --> 05:20.920
Well, you're more polite than I thought.

05:20.920 --> 05:24.820
For being members of the
World Destruction Committee, that is.

05:24.820 --> 05:28.780
I saw this posted at the harbor
where I stopped this morning.

05:31.560 --> 05:34.100
W-Wait a minute! I'm not...!

05:34.100 --> 05:36.100
I'm not either, bear-o!

05:36.100 --> 05:38.500
Hey c'mon, don't get so worked up about it!

05:38.500 --> 05:40.900
I'm not your enemy.

05:40.900 --> 05:42.900
I'm just Agan the smuggler.

05:42.900 --> 05:45.570
You got the money, I'll carry anything you want.

05:45.570 --> 05:49.240
Even outlaws from the
World Destruction Committee.

05:49.240 --> 05:51.780
Which is to say, how much will you give me?

05:51.780 --> 05:53.850
Is that a threat?

05:53.850 --> 05:56.990
Don't forget we're the
World Destruction Committee.

05:56.990 --> 05:59.290
Like I was saying, it's not really we, so...

05:59.290 --> 06:02.520
How long are you planning
to hang onto that, anyway? Give it back.

06:02.520 --> 06:05.190
So that's the Destruct Code?

06:06.330 --> 06:09.700
I heard stories about it when I was a kid.

06:09.700 --> 06:15.800
The legend of the secret treasure with the
power to destroy the world... the Destruct Code.

06:15.800 --> 06:18.810
Supposedly it's hidden somewhere in the world.

06:18.810 --> 06:21.140
Some say it lies sunken at
the bottom of the Sand Sea.

06:21.140 --> 06:26.010
Others say it lies buried under
the thick ice of the winter continent.

06:26.010 --> 06:29.450
But if that thing is the real Destruct Code,

06:29.450 --> 06:31.550
then you three are sitting
on one whopper of a treasure!

06:31.550 --> 06:34.290
Don't touch it! Of course it's the real thing!

06:34.290 --> 06:37.190
Yeah, but all she does is just talk
about bringing about world destruction.

06:37.190 --> 06:39.130
She doesn't actually know how to use it.

06:39.130 --> 06:42.200
And you can shut your mouth!

06:42.200 --> 06:46.500
Well, if you don't even know how to use it,
how do you know it's the real thing?

06:46.500 --> 06:49.560
The person who had it before me would never lie.

06:59.550 --> 07:01.180
All right, whatever you say.

07:01.180 --> 07:02.680
I'll take your word for it.

07:02.680 --> 07:08.320
And in exchange for that Destruct Code, I'll
take you anywhere in the world you want to go!

07:08.320 --> 07:10.530
I can't give you the Destruct Code.

07:10.530 --> 07:13.030
In that case, I'll take cash.

07:13.030 --> 07:15.330
This is all we have right now.

07:15.330 --> 07:16.930
If that's all you've got,

07:16.930 --> 07:20.100
the only thing you can buy from me is
one of these cans of sand whale meat.

07:20.100 --> 07:22.000
Fine!

07:22.000 --> 07:24.010
Here's where I step in
and take care of it, bear-o.

07:24.010 --> 07:27.240
Who's there? Where are you?

07:27.240 --> 07:28.610
I'm here, bear-o!

07:28.610 --> 07:30.110
And I will take care of this, bear-o!

07:30.110 --> 07:33.080
What's the story with this bear? It can talk?

07:33.080 --> 07:34.750
Don't call me a bear, bear-o!

07:34.750 --> 07:36.940
But you are a bear.

07:37.020 --> 07:39.250
B-Bear... o...

07:43.260 --> 07:46.860
Well, all right then! For this
I'll go ahead and take you guys.

07:46.860 --> 07:51.420
I'm delivering a load to the
pleasure ship Jifnil anyway, so why not.

08:09.880 --> 08:11.390
So what's a pleasure ship?

08:11.390 --> 08:12.790
Just what it sounds like...

08:12.790 --> 08:17.460
a ship that offers up anything in the
world that you might call "pleasure."

08:17.460 --> 08:21.330
From illegal casinos to bars
stocked with beautiful women.

08:21.330 --> 08:24.470
Even secret nightclubs that
are normally off-limits to minors.

08:24.470 --> 08:26.330
The ship has got literally everything.

08:36.110 --> 08:38.250
Well, that's all of it.

08:38.250 --> 08:40.920
I guess the only thing left is you three.

08:40.920 --> 08:42.520
Hurry up and get off.

08:42.520 --> 08:44.490
What? Here?!

08:44.490 --> 08:46.690
Hey, this is as far as you
go for what you paid me.

08:46.690 --> 08:49.020
Looks like you're going the rest
of the way on the pleasure ship.

08:49.020 --> 08:50.690
Is this some kind of trick, bear-o?

08:50.690 --> 08:53.130
C'mon, don't be like that.

08:53.130 --> 08:55.200
This pleasure ship is an outlaw zone.

08:55.200 --> 08:57.470
Beastmen, humans...
none of that matters here.

08:57.470 --> 09:01.270
In other words, it's the perfect place for
a bunch of fugitives such as yourselves

09:01.270 --> 09:03.670
to hide from the law.

09:03.670 --> 09:06.140
Well, it sounds like fun to me. Off we go!

09:06.140 --> 09:07.810
B-B-B-Bear-o...

09:07.810 --> 09:10.210
C'mon, you too. Get going!

09:16.620 --> 09:17.720
See ya later!

09:17.720 --> 09:20.660
And next time we meet, bring more money!

09:20.660 --> 09:23.780
Then I can take you wherever you want!

09:44.050 --> 09:45.550
Hey there, little bear!

09:45.550 --> 09:47.520
We've got lots of nice young
girls in here. Stop in for a drink?

09:47.520 --> 09:49.580
I'm good, bear-o.

09:49.580 --> 09:51.690
The last thing we need

09:51.690 --> 09:53.720
is to hang around in some seedy club
and get ourselves in more trouble, bear-o.

09:53.720 --> 09:55.660
If we're smart, we'll lay
low and mind our own business

09:55.660 --> 09:58.030
until this ship pulls into
port somewhere, bear-o.

09:58.030 --> 09:59.330
Sure, whatever.

09:59.330 --> 10:02.560
But don't you think it's about time you stopped
saying "bear-o" at the end of every sentence?

10:02.560 --> 10:03.830
That's a good point.

10:03.830 --> 10:06.070
I mean, your voice sounds
pretty cool when you don't say that.

10:06.070 --> 10:07.900
That's one thing I cannot do, bear-o.

10:07.900 --> 10:11.200
That word is a proud
symbol of our tribe, bear-o.

10:22.050 --> 10:24.520
Oh, I'm sorry.

10:24.520 --> 10:26.890
What's a little girl like
that doing on a pleasure ship?

10:26.890 --> 10:28.380
Beats me.

10:33.460 --> 10:34.950
Enter.

10:36.300 --> 10:39.470
Who the hell are you people?

10:39.470 --> 10:41.200
It's a pleasure to meet you.

10:41.200 --> 10:44.110
We're from the World Salvation
Committee. My name is Nadja...

10:44.110 --> 10:46.410
and this is Lia.

10:46.410 --> 10:48.240
The others work for us.

10:48.240 --> 10:52.750
So? What the hell's the World
Salvation Committee doing on my ship?

10:52.750 --> 10:54.980
Some members of the
World Destruction Committee

10:54.980 --> 10:58.050
recently disappeared in
a nearby area of the sea.

10:58.050 --> 11:00.590
There's a possibility that they
may be hiding out on board this ship.

11:00.590 --> 11:03.790
If you find them on board, we'd like
you to hand them over to our custody.

11:03.790 --> 11:05.280
I'll do no such thing.

11:08.300 --> 11:09.930
What exactly are you saying?

11:09.930 --> 11:13.230
On board this ship, beastmen or
humans or criminals... makes no difference.

11:13.230 --> 11:17.440
There's just one place on the
planet that's not under anyone's control...

11:17.440 --> 11:20.470
and that's right here,
on the pleasure ship Jifnil.

11:20.470 --> 11:23.440
So if you want to look around, then be my guest.

11:23.440 --> 11:26.450
We won't get in your way, but
don't expect any help from us, either.

11:26.450 --> 11:30.180
I see. That should suit us just fine.

11:42.130 --> 11:44.000
- This is good!
- Really?

11:44.000 --> 11:47.590
- What about this one?
- Which one? Oh, that is good!

11:49.800 --> 11:52.170
I finally opened the can of sand whale!

11:52.170 --> 11:54.640
And here you go...
I borrowed a bottle opener for you.

11:55.680 --> 11:57.440
Hold on... where's Morte?

11:58.550 --> 12:01.180
I'm sure she was here until just a minute ago.

12:01.180 --> 12:03.010
Guess she's not here now, bear-o.

12:11.490 --> 12:13.130
Looks like you're winning every round.

12:13.130 --> 12:16.030
Of course I am!
My luck's about as good as it gets.

12:16.030 --> 12:18.670
There's no way I could've made
it this far alive without good luck.

12:18.670 --> 12:21.570
Now I'd like to place all of it on black.

12:21.570 --> 12:23.240
Is that your bet?

12:23.240 --> 12:24.470
Very well.

12:31.550 --> 12:33.240
It seems we found her.

12:35.520 --> 12:36.820
You have to wait, Lia.

12:36.820 --> 12:38.720
Why are you stopping me, Nadja?

12:38.720 --> 12:41.190
When you're on Jifnil,
do things the Jifnil way.

12:41.190 --> 12:45.350
Since we're here on this ship, let's do
things the way they do them, shall we?

12:51.900 --> 12:54.940
There's no sense running around
the ship looking for her, bear-o.

12:54.940 --> 12:57.870
After all, it's not like we're
her friends or anything, bear-o.

12:57.870 --> 13:00.410
But we did come all this way together...

13:00.410 --> 13:03.110
and what if something's happened to her?

13:03.110 --> 13:05.780
Well, sounds to me like you
might have a crush, eh bear-o?

13:05.780 --> 13:08.050
Huh? Did you say something?

13:08.050 --> 13:09.550
Never mind, bear-o.

13:09.550 --> 13:12.920
The point is, there's no reason for us to
stay involved with that girl any longer, bear-o.

13:12.920 --> 13:16.390
But we're in a casino... she could
be getting ripped off as we speak!

13:16.390 --> 13:20.260
That girl isn't the kind of gal who'll
just take a fleecing lying down, bear-o.

13:20.260 --> 13:22.960
And besides, she seems
ungodly lucky in competition, bear-o.

13:22.960 --> 13:24.260
Still...

13:27.800 --> 13:29.460
I seem to have underestimated you.

13:33.610 --> 13:34.710
Greetings, madam.

13:34.710 --> 13:36.710
It appears that goddesses of good fortune

13:36.710 --> 13:40.940
from all over the world have
gathered around you this evening.

13:42.980 --> 13:47.480
How about it? Would you like to
play a game of cards with me next?

13:51.060 --> 13:53.490
There are two kinds of women, bear-o.

13:53.490 --> 13:55.660
Women who can get by just fine on their own...

13:55.660 --> 13:57.330
and women who can't.

13:57.330 --> 14:00.330
Morte is one of the ones who
can get by on her own, bear-o.

14:00.330 --> 14:04.110
So you're saying that just because she can
get by on her own, we don't need to help her?

14:04.110 --> 14:05.610
You're supposed to be a hero.

14:05.610 --> 14:07.940
Heroes got places to be, bear-o.

14:07.940 --> 14:11.670
There are always plenty of
other people in need of help, bear-o.

14:14.320 --> 14:15.480
Oh, that girl from before.

14:15.480 --> 14:18.490
A little girl like that is exactly
the type who needs a hero, bear-o.

14:18.490 --> 14:20.190
Now hurry and get her attention, bear-o!

14:20.190 --> 14:22.520
Me?! Why?

14:22.520 --> 14:24.790
Just do it already, bear-o.

14:27.360 --> 14:29.930
Um, excuse me. Is everything all right?

14:29.930 --> 14:32.800
This isn't the safest place for
a young girl to be walking alo...

14:34.800 --> 14:37.140
What's your problem? Leave me alone.

14:37.140 --> 14:39.440
I don't see how my affairs
are any of your business.

14:39.440 --> 14:42.810
Um, isn't this probably one of
the girls who can get by on her own?

14:42.810 --> 14:44.480
Now wait, bear-o.

14:44.480 --> 14:46.850
If there's something going on,
then just tell us, bear-o.

14:46.850 --> 14:49.320
You never know...
we might be able to help, bear-o.

14:49.320 --> 14:50.650
What's up with this bear?

14:50.650 --> 14:52.120
Don't call me a bear, bear-o!

14:52.120 --> 14:56.720
Whoa, whoa. Maybe she's
just out looking for someone.

14:57.560 --> 14:59.630
I came here to bring my father back.

14:59.630 --> 15:04.030
He got hooked on gambling
and spent all his time on this ship.

15:04.030 --> 15:07.700
But he racked up a mountain of
debt and now they're holding him here.

15:07.700 --> 15:09.500
Well, that's...

15:09.500 --> 15:12.740
That's what we call serves him right, bear-o.

15:12.740 --> 15:15.510
If you really wanna help, then gimme some money.

15:15.510 --> 15:17.810
I can use it to get him back.

15:17.810 --> 15:19.210
We don't have any money, bear-o.

15:19.210 --> 15:21.350
In that case, you're useless to me.

15:21.350 --> 15:23.250
Hey, wait!

15:28.560 --> 15:29.260
Oh crap!

15:29.260 --> 15:30.420
Bear-o!

15:41.840 --> 15:44.540
So, what are you going to do?

15:44.540 --> 15:46.010
I'll stand.

15:46.010 --> 15:47.200
Very well.

16:03.090 --> 16:09.260
Unlike roulette, card games require
cool-headed decisions and careful analysis.

16:09.260 --> 16:11.470
You can't win on luck alone.

16:11.470 --> 16:13.230
You have to use this too.

16:13.230 --> 16:16.370
Are you suggesting I'm not using my brain?!

16:16.370 --> 16:20.470
I'm saying nothing of the sort.
Shall we play another hand?

16:20.470 --> 16:24.550
Of course! Just you watch...
I'll get it all back with this one.

16:24.550 --> 16:28.070
That's quite a wager! Are you sure?

16:37.590 --> 16:42.090
It seems the goddesses of good
fortune have come over to my side.

16:45.270 --> 16:48.390
So then, all of this becomes mine now.

16:52.110 --> 16:56.280
What do you say? Try and
win it all back with one last hand?

16:56.280 --> 16:59.450
You've cleaned me out.
I don't even have one silver coin left.

16:59.450 --> 17:03.350
In that case, perhaps something
of yours other than money?

17:03.350 --> 17:10.320
Ah yes. For example, you could
wager the Destruct Code, Morte Urshela!

17:10.320 --> 17:13.430
If you win, all of this money will be yours.

17:13.430 --> 17:17.800
If you lose, the Destruct Code is mine.

17:17.800 --> 17:19.430
This is taking forever!

17:19.430 --> 17:22.440
I don't know why we have to
keep pussy-footing around...

17:22.440 --> 17:25.040
when we could just grab what
we want by force and be done with it!

17:25.040 --> 17:29.440
An intriguing offer.
Very well, I accept your challenge!

17:29.440 --> 17:31.380
Music to my ears.

17:33.710 --> 17:35.480
What the...?!

17:35.980 --> 17:38.680
Is there a problem? Are you backing out?

17:40.320 --> 17:43.380
Not on your life. Let's play!

17:53.300 --> 17:55.000
Where's my father?!

17:56.400 --> 17:58.840
I want my father back!

18:01.040 --> 18:03.710
Heh, what a sassy young thing you are.

18:03.710 --> 18:06.980
I don't mind giving him back to you,
but what about the debt he owes?

18:06.980 --> 18:09.480
You have that kind of money, little girl?

18:09.480 --> 18:12.480
Money no, but I do have something else to offer.

18:13.890 --> 18:17.220
It's a priceless treasure,
with the power to destroy the world...

18:17.220 --> 18:19.430
the Destruct Code!

18:19.430 --> 18:21.560
Hey, what?! That's mine!

18:21.560 --> 18:23.660
You, where'd you get that?!

18:27.270 --> 18:28.890
This was your bet?

18:38.080 --> 18:40.010
Not bad for a kid!

18:42.080 --> 18:43.520
Freeze!

18:47.220 --> 18:48.960
Ow!

18:48.960 --> 18:50.890
Oh hey, sand whale!

18:55.900 --> 19:00.030
This is why I said we should've
just grabbed it by force in the first place!

19:04.300 --> 19:07.270
You stupid little brat!

19:17.380 --> 19:21.320
Hand it over. Give me the Destruct Code.

19:52.350 --> 19:53.790
Kyrie!

19:53.790 --> 19:55.310
Lia!

20:11.710 --> 20:14.480
We gotta get going now, bear-o!

20:14.480 --> 20:15.970
Come with us!

20:17.780 --> 20:19.110
I'm not going.

20:19.110 --> 20:21.220
I have to save my father first.

20:21.220 --> 20:23.680
You can come back and save him later!

20:23.680 --> 20:25.450
Right now we should just get out of here!

20:25.450 --> 20:27.120
I'm not scared.

20:27.120 --> 20:31.490
Besides, they're after the World Destruction
Committee, which is you guys, isn't it?

20:31.490 --> 20:34.160
She's right. Let's go!

20:34.160 --> 20:35.720
Yeah, but...

20:37.870 --> 20:40.700
You can sell that for at least one silver coin.

20:40.700 --> 20:43.000
I can't give you the Destruct Code,

20:43.000 --> 20:46.370
but you can use the coin as seed
money to help get your father back.

20:47.570 --> 20:49.300
Thank you.

20:59.390 --> 21:01.760
We let them slip through our fingers.

21:01.760 --> 21:04.090
I'm sorry. It was my fault.

21:04.090 --> 21:10.000
"World Destruction"...
why destruction, I wonder.

21:10.000 --> 21:12.760
They've piqued my curiosity.

21:25.010 --> 21:27.410
All right then, I'll be going now.

21:27.410 --> 21:30.180
Sorry to get you two mixed up in this.

21:30.180 --> 21:31.380
Bear-o?

21:33.020 --> 21:35.060
Hey, wait a minute!

21:35.060 --> 21:38.360
You can't just leave us stranded like this!

21:38.360 --> 21:40.590
Oh... so you're coming with me, then?

21:40.590 --> 21:42.900
Well, that's not exactly what I meant...

21:42.900 --> 21:46.530
but me and Toppy are both fugitives now, so...

21:46.530 --> 21:50.700
Well if you want to come
along, have it your way.

21:50.700 --> 21:53.740
I have an idea! Why don't we
quit all that world destruction stuff

21:53.740 --> 21:56.240
and just go around helping
people like this instead?

21:56.240 --> 22:00.550
I mean, we always seem to wind up
helping someone in the end, anyway.

22:00.550 --> 22:06.490
The way this world is, we'd be
helping everyone by destroying it for them.

22:06.490 --> 22:08.290
What are you gonna do, Toppy?

22:08.290 --> 22:12.620
For now I think I'll just help
you guys out a bit longer, bear-o.

22:21.130 --> 22:24.640
Kirameku suna no umi

22:24.640 --> 22:27.770
Aoi chijou no hate

22:27.770 --> 22:33.850
Yuuyami ni ochita sora kara

22:33.850 --> 22:36.980
afuredasu kioku

22:36.980 --> 22:40.190
Gareki no you ni

22:40.190 --> 22:46.190
kasanete yuku darou

22:46.190 --> 22:49.430
Meguriau inochi

22:49.430 --> 22:52.500
Surechigau kimochi

22:52.500 --> 22:55.640
Tsumugiau kotoba

22:55.640 --> 22:58.770
Kizutsukeau mono

22:58.770 --> 23:10.880
Sore demo bokura ga aruiteku
michi wa asu e tsuzuiteru no

23:13.720 --> 23:17.560
Ima o against the world ikiru imi wa

23:17.560 --> 23:20.560
change the world hitotsu janai

23:20.560 --> 23:26.130
Namima no mukou haruka na tabi e

23:26.130 --> 23:29.700
Dakara around the world ikiru kodou

23:29.700 --> 23:33.240
To the end of the world kaze ni hibike

23:33.240 --> 23:39.210
Sono saki ni aru

23:39.210 --> 23:50.820
yakusoku no chi, tadoritsukeru made

23:52.190 --> 23:54.830
I don't know what happened, but we got captured!

23:54.830 --> 23:59.930
We found ourselves locked up in a
notorious prison run by a bunch of wolves!

23:59.930 --> 24:02.040
And we have to find some way to escape...

24:02.040 --> 24:04.770
Before those two from the
World Salvation Committee get here!

24:04.770 --> 24:07.940
Next time on World Destruction... Episode 3:

24:07.940 --> 24:10.080
"There Are Two Kinds of Beastmen."

24:10.080 --> 24:11.610
Hey, where's Toppy?

24:11.610 --> 24:13.950
He's over there sulking.

24:13.950 --> 24:16.280
A hero in prison!

24:16.280 --> 24:19.120
What's the world coming to... bear-o?
